  "body_html": "<h1>Single-Block Lattice Transfer</h1>\n<p>Let \\(w\\in\\operatorname{Hom}_D(V,V')\\) satisfy \\(M(w)\\in\\Gamma+\\mathbf g_{x,r+}\\) for a single positive-depth block of depth \\(r=2s\\). Define\n\\[\nL'_t=wL_{t+s}.\n\\]\nThen \\(L'\\) is self-dual, its jumps are the jumps of \\(L\\) shifted by \\(-s\\), and it is the unique self-dual lattice function with \\(w\\in (L\\otimes L')_s\\).</p>",
  "proof_html": "<p>The proof computes dual lattices using \\(w^\\ast w=M(w)\\), the relation \\(\\Gamma L_{t+s}=L_{t-s}\\), and self-duality of \\(L\\). Uniqueness follows by comparing a candidate lattice function with \\(wL_{t+s}\\) and then dualizing the inclusion.</p>",
